[size=6][b]QoLar Expanse[/b][/size]

Quality-of-life fixes for Solar Expanse: jump around the solar system with hotkeys, open any screen with one key, and tame the cargo panel, all without changing how the game actually plays.

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Solar-system navigation.[/b] Step between planets in distance-from-sun order and between a planet's moons with Ctrl + arrow keys, favorited bodies included as extra stops. Ctrl-click a body to snap between its surface and orbital view. Dragging behaves the same everywhere, too: whether you pick something up from the bottom nav bar or from a 3D body in the view, holding Ctrl while you drag cargo onto a body drops it into that body's orbit.[/*]
[*][b]One-key screens.[/b] F4 through F7 open Search, Missions, Market, and Research directly; with a body selected, Missions and Market open for that body. The arrow keys also stop nudging the map while you type or have a screen open, so a shortcut or a stray letter won't drag the camera by accident.[/*]
[*][b]Mission-planning shortcuts.[/b] Inside the Plan Mission window, toggle origin or destination between surface and orbit, swap them, and step back and forward, all from the keyboard. The mnemonic: A is your point A (origin), D is your destination, and S, sitting between them, swaps the two.[/*]
[*][b]Quick save and load.[/b] One key writes a fresh save, another reloads your most recent one, with an on-screen confirmation.[/*]
[*][b]Calmer contract loading.[/b] Loading a save full of contracts no longer spams a popup and a sound for every restored contract.[/*]
[*][b]A tidier cargo panel.[/b] Identical modules collapse into one row with a quantity you can edit directly, a Drop All button clears leftover cargo in one click, and every module row stays editable so you can add or swap any module whenever you like.[/*]
[*][b]Ships as tiles, not rows.[/b] A body's ships and launch vehicles show up as square icon tiles matching the facility and module tiles, instead of a full-width row each, so a developed body's whole panel fits without scrolling. A tile standing for several ships of one type carries the count in its corner, the same way a facility tile does. Everything still works from the tile: drag it to plan a mission or reorder the build queue, click it for the full ship screen, watch the build shade fill, and cancel a single ship in progress with the X in its corner. The row's small info button goes with the labels, so the type preview it used to open is no longer reachable; a plain click on the tile opens the full ship screen, which says everything that preview did and lets you delete the ship as well.[/*]
[/list]

